    "result_text": "All 266 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. (The lone `GeneralExceptionHandler - Unexpected error` line is from a pre-existing error-path test in `UserRestControllerV1Tests`, which still reports 0 failures.)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required the owner response to include a computed `displayName` field formatted as `LastName, FirstName`. The new `Cp06Tests.coreDisplayName` reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the field must appear on the owner response generally, not just at creation.\n\nTwo changes, both driving off the existing generated-DTO + MapStruct pipeline:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits the field on `OwnerDto`. Read-only keeps it out of request binding (`OwnerFields` is untouched).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 annotated `toOwnerDto` with `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")`, so every owner response (create via `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, read via `RespondWithOwner`, and list mappings) carries the derived value.\n\nNo changes to the OfficeFloor function pipeline or YAML were needed \u2014 the responders already map through `OwnerMapper`.",
